# integrations/claude-code/drive, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3):
# evaluating this directory yields the image that runs drive.go as a worker.
#
# std/go's /worker `go run`s whatever is bound as `worker1`. drive.go REFUSES
# to run outside a worker, so this entry is the only way to reach the verbs. It
# reads its arguments from /cas/args and its token from
# /secret/claude-oauth-token — minted by authorize.go beside it, which runs on
# the HOST because it needs a browser and a paste (see README.md) — and it
# imports nothing outside the standard library, so the prelude module std/go
# copies beside it is never consulted.
#
# NOTHING IS BOUND HERE. A caller curries the verb, its arguments, and the time:
#
#   caos-cli run --base:@=integrations/claude-code/drive \
#     --verb=list --at="$(date +%s)"
#   caos-cli run --base:@=integrations/claude-code/drive --verb=start \
#     --env=Caos --repo=Metta-AI/caos-session --prompt='the first prompt' \
#     --at="$(date +%s)"
#
# The prompt is a plain string argument. `:@=` would ingest a FILE, and it
# ingests only git-tracked paths — an ad-hoc prompt is not one.
#
# `at` IS REQUIRED BY EVERY VERB. A worker's result is memoized on its ArgTree
# and nothing here is a pure function of its arguments, so without a value that
# moves, a second `start` answers with the first session's id and creates
# nothing, and a second `list` answers with a listing from whenever the first
# one ran. A coarser time (`date +%Y%m%d%H%M`) deliberately reuses an answer.
#
# THE HELP IS BOUND HERE, so this describes itself to any harness offering it
# and there is no second copy to drift (the note std/merge/.caos-expr carries,
# for the same reason). The description is joined into ONE line by `parse_help`,
# so it is prose rather than a table.
#
# `at` is a parameter a model must fill, and that is deliberate: it is what
# makes the call reach the API rather than the memo. `salt` is a RESERVED arg
# name and could not have been used for it.
#
# No `@writer` and no `@in`: nothing here advances the conversation tree.
HELP=<<END
Start and inspect Claude Code cloud sessions. A session runs in a named cloud
environment, on a named GitHub repository, and answers prompts. `verb` chooses
what to do, and the other parameters belong to the verb: `start` takes env, repo
and prompt and returns a session id; `send` takes session and prompt; `list`
takes nothing and returns recent sessions with their status and environment;
`info` takes session and returns its environment, its source and its
provisioning trace; `conv` takes session and locates the caos conversation it
records into; `archive` takes session and ends it, freeing its container.
Environments are separately addressable: `env-list` takes nothing, `env-show`
takes env, and `env-update`, `env-create` and `env-delete` CHANGE, CREATE and
DESTROY an environment that other sessions may be using. A session id is
`cse_...` or `session_...`, two spellings of the same session, and either is
accepted wherever one is asked for. Starting a session costs a container and
about two minutes before it can answer, so read the reply back with `info`
rather than expecting one from `start`.
@param verb One of start, send, list, info, conv, archive, env-list, env-show, env-update, env-create, env-delete.
@param at The current time as seconds since the epoch. The result is memoized on the arguments, so a value used before returns that earlier answer instead of asking again — pass the time now, not a constant.
@param {string} [env] Cloud environment, by name or by its env_... id.
@param {string} [repo] Repository the session opens: owner/repo, owner/repo@ref, or a full URL.
@param {string} [prompt] Prompt text, for start and send.
@param {string} [session] Session id (cse_... or session_...) or a claude.ai/code URL.
@param {string} [ref] Branch, tag or commit to check out; the repository's default when omitted.
@param {string} [title] The session's title; the prompt's first line when omitted.
@param {string} [from] env-create only: an existing environment to copy.
@param {string} [rename] env-update only: a new name for the environment.
@param {string} [init-script] env-update only: the environment's new setup script, in full.
@param {array} [set-env] env-update only: environment variables to set, each as KEY=VALUE.
@param {array} [unset-env] env-update only: names of environment variables to remove.
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/go --worker1:@=drive.go --help=$HELP
